                    ],
                    "text": "br.shaper"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-2",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [
                        15.0,
                        40.0,
                        760.0,
                        20.0
                    ],
                    "text": "Mono waveshapers in gen~ for synthesis: fold, wrap, clip and buchla (sine fold), one abstraction each, plus br.shaper.multi with all four."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [
                        15.0,
                        65.0,
                        988.0,
                        20.0
                    ],
                    "text": "Every abstraction has the inlets Input, Drive, Mix (multi adds Mode). Hover an inlet for its range and default. Drive pushes the signal harder into the shape; Mix blends back the dry input."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-4",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [
                        15.0,
                        90.0,
                        1006.0,
                        20.0
                    ],
                    "text": "Antialiased (1st-order ADAA), so high drive doesn't fill the spectrum with aliasing. Drive and Mix glide 10 ms; multi's Mode crossfades 20 ms. No DC filter, so LFOs pass through untouched."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-5",
                    "linecount": 4,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [
                        15.0,
                        120.0,
                        331.0,
                        60.0
                    ],
                    "text": "Tabs:\n  singles: the four shapers side by side, with a listen menu\n  multi: all four in one, with the Mode menu\n  lfo: a slow sine shaped by multi, shown on a scope"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
